From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Infante de Castro <18445184+fidecastro@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:12:10 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: romulus15: enable the Iris video codec

video-codec@aa00000 is disabled on the Surface Laptop 7 15", so it has
no hardware video decode or encode. Enable it and name its firmware next
to the laptop's other DSP firmware.

The firmware has to be signed by Microsoft. qcvss8380.mbn from the
Surface Pro 11's driver package loads on this laptop.

Tested on the Surface Laptop 7 15": the decoder and encoder devices
appear, the decoder lists H.264, HEVC, VP9 and AV1, and a 1080p H.264
clip decodes through h264_v4l2m2m to the same frames as software decode.

Assisted-by: Claude Fable 5.2
Signed-off-by: Felipe Infante de Castro <18445184+fidecastro@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts    | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
index 023cc02..a8e7634 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/x1e80100-microsoft-romulus15.dts
@@ -102,3 +102,14 @@
 		bias-disable;
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * The video codec needs Microsoft-signed firmware. qcvss8380.mbn from the
+ * Surface Pro 11's driver package is accepted on this laptop. It loads on
+ * first use; until then, opening the device fails.
+ */
+&iris {
+	firmware-name = "qcom/x1e80100/microsoft/Romulus/qcvss8380.mbn";
+
+	status = "okay";
+};
